    "Details": "Power Drain: -40\n\n    Deathfire Rockets are heavy-hitting, long-range rockets with explosive warheads that function much like LRMs.  They can be used for indirect fire with the help of a spotter.  Small and compact compared to SRM and LRM missiles, they don't take up a lot of space, and are made out of high-tech materials that make them lightweight.\n\n    These weapons come in different type levels (Type 1, Type 2, etc.).  Weapons of a higher level have increased damage, range, and accuracy, but also draw more continual power from a battlemech's engine and power systems, which result in lower maximum heat and heat shutdown thresholds for the battlemech."
